Q: Proxies with Python &#39;Requests&#39; module A: <p>The accepted answer was a good start for me, but I kept getting the following error:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>AssertionError: Not supported proxy scheme None</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The fix to this was to specify the <em>http://</em> in the proxy URL, thus:</p>
<pre><code>http_proxy  = &quot;http://194.62.145.248:8080&quot;
https_proxy = &quot;https://194.62.145.248:8080&quot;
ftp_proxy   = &quot;10.10.1.10:3128&quot;

proxyDict = {
              &quot;http&quot;  : http_proxy,
              &quot;https&quot; : https_proxy,
              &quot;ftp&quot;   : ftp_proxy
            }
</code></pre>
<p>I'd be interested as to why the original works for some people, but not me.</p>
<p>The main answer is now updated to reflect this :)</p>
